  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Framework with the United Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction (UNDRR) 2022-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction (UNDRR) is the UN agency overseeing implementation of the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030. It supports countries to implement the Sendai Framework (and the Sendai Gender Action Plan, which shares best practice) to prevent new and reduce existing disaster risks and to strengthen resilience through a multi-hazard approach to disaster risk management. UNDRR also supports strengthening inclusivity and resilience through the Early Warnings for All Initiative. This investment&#x2019;s core funding enables UNDRR to implement its Strategic Partnership Framework with Australia, the approach and objectives of which include mobilising advocacy and knowledge sharing for risk-informed sustainable development; capacity building to increase the availability of risk data and information; and strengthening inclusive disaster resilience in the Pacific reg of the partnership also support UNDRR&#x2019;s work in the Indo-Pacific region.</narrative>
  </description>
